# Backend
jarvis-backend/venv/
jarvis-backend/__pycache__/
jarvis-backend/logs/
jarvis-backend/jarvis_chroma_db/
jarvis-backend/credentials/
*.pyc

# --- Large model binaries (re-downloadable — see README "Fresh Install") ---
jarvis-backend/models/vosk/
jarvis-backend/*.onnx
jarvis-backend/*.onnx.json
jarvis-backend/*.pt
jarvis-backend/*.tar.gz

# --- Personal memory / RAG stores (auto-created; never commit) ---
jarvis-backend/*.db
# In-flight migration copies and sqlite sidecars. `*.db` above does NOT cover
# these: `jarvis_longterm.db.sourcing-<stamp>` does not END in `.db`. A verify
# that fails leaves one on disk on purpose, and it holds the same rows the live
# store does — it must not be one `git add -A` away from being published.
jarvis-backend/*.db.*
jarvis-backend/*.db-wal
jarvis-backend/*.db-shm
jarvis-backend/memory/vector_db/
jarvis-backend/personal_chroma_db/
jarvis-backend/action_chroma_db/

# --- The same stores, WHEREVER they land ---
# Every pattern above is anchored to jarvis-backend/, which is right for the real
# stores and useless the moment one is created somewhere else. Chroma paths used
# to be taken relative to the process's CWD, so launching from the repo root
# produced an UNIGNORED jarvis_chroma_db/ at the top level — holding the
# plaintext vector mirror of facts that are ciphertext in jarvis_longterm.db, one
# `git add -A` away from being published. memory.py is anchored now; these
# unanchored patterns are the belt to that braces, because the next stray store
# will be created by something nobody has thought of yet.
jarvis_chroma_db/
personal_chroma_db/
action_chroma_db/
rag_chroma_db/
vector_db/

# --- And their MIGRATION COPIES ---
# The patterns above end in a slash and match the directory NAME exactly, so
# `jarvis_chroma_db.plaintext-20260816-120052/` — the copy that
# migrate_chroma_encryption.py takes aside before sealing anything — matched
# none of them and showed up as untracked. That folder is the LAST plaintext
# copy of the 118 memory documents on this machine, which is precisely the
# thing that migration exists to remove from the disk, and it was one
# `git add -A` from being published. This file already records that exact
# mistake happening once (run_evals.py, commit 9b12df6).
*_chroma_db.*/
*_chroma_db.*
jarvis-backend/*_chroma_db.*/

# --- Agent measurement (§6.8.4) — counters, per machine, never shared ---
# It stores no argument values and no goal text by construction, but it is still
# a record of how this particular desk is used, and it is per-machine noise in a
# diff. `run_evals.py --metrics` reads it locally.
jarvis-backend/metrics/

# --- External MCP servers (§6.8.3) — whose config names local paths and may
# --- carry an env block. Never committed: the example lives in the roadmap.
jarvis-backend/mcp_servers.json

# --- TTS scratch (F-14) — a synthesis leaves its mp3 behind in the backend
# --- root; they are per-utterance noise and one was found untracked mid-gate.
jarvis-backend/temp_speech_*.mp3

# --- Memory encryption keys (C#11a) — losing these loses the memory ---
jarvis-backend/jarvis_key.*
jarvis-backend/jarvis_x25519.enc

# --- Sealed-fact queue runtime state (C#11a Step 4) — never commit any of it.
# fact_quarantine/  records that failed to open, kept for inspection
# fact_outbox.jsonl the cloud-side spill: sealed envelopes awaiting the desk
# fact_desk_key.json the cached desk PUBLIC half (not secret, but not ours to
#                    publish either — it names the key his facts are sealed to)
# The ledger is a *.db and already covered above. ---
jarvis-backend/fact_quarantine/
jarvis-backend/fact_outbox.jsonl
jarvis-backend/fact_desk_key.json

# --- Test/tooling caches ---
jarvis-backend/.pytest_cache/

# --- Runtime artifacts ---
jarvis-backend/watchdog.log
# Live-gate console captures. Kept on disk as the session's raw record and NOT
# committed: they carry real inbox previews (senders and subject lines) and the
# watchdog's session shutdown token.
jarvis-backend/gate-s4-*.log
jarvis-backend/gate-session-*.log
jarvis-backend/desk.log
jarvis-backend/desk.err.log
jarvis-backend/error.log
jarvis-backend/last_boot_date.txt
jarvis-backend/test_grid_output.jpg

# Frontend
jarvis-frontend/node_modules/
jarvis-frontend/dist/

# OS Files
.DS_Store
.env
KEys.txt

# Runtime state the gateway persists, per install: push addresses registered by
# the phone app, the commute schedule it uploads, which briefings already went
# out, and the last unprompted nudge. The .test.json ones are written by
# test_app_link.py, which points every one of these at its own copy.
jarvis-backend/app_push_tokens.json
jarvis-backend/app_push_tokens.test.json
jarvis-backend/app_commute.json
jarvis-backend/app_commute.test.json
jarvis-backend/app_briefed.json
jarvis-backend/app_briefed.test.json
jarvis-backend/app_nudge.json
jarvis-backend/app_nudge.test.json
jarvis-backend/app_voice.json
jarvis-backend/app_voice.test.json

# the vite dev server log, when the HUD is run for a gate session
jarvis-backend/hud-dev.log
